 seemed  to have used an eight day week in their  earlier period and only adopted the  seven day week later making it official  during the rule of constantine  they adopted it as with so many things  from the greeks who in turn got it from  both the mesopotamians and the  israelites probably during alexander the  great's empire anyway the romans took  the seven day week and copied the greeks  and babylonians by naming the days after  their planets which were in turn named  for their gods  the romans spread their culture  including their weak all throughout  their empire  and even into the germanic tribes one of  which were the anglo-saxons who were the  first english speakers though their  language sounds very different from ours  used in a process scholars call  interpretatio germanica the germanic  people substituted some of their deities  for the roman deities  sunday and monday stayed the same so  diaz solis became sunindeg eventually  sunday  and diaz lunai became monandeg  eventually monday  the third day of the roman week was  named diaz martis named for mars the  roman god of war so the anglo-saxons  chose the one-handed god of combat tyr  so tiwa's dag meaning tears day  eventually evolved to tuesday  dies mercury was the next day named for  the messenger god mercury the  anglo-saxons somewhat strangely chose  vodin called odin by the norsemen the  all-father and king of the gods as their  replacement both deities have links to  magic and knowledge which is presumably  why they were seen as equivalent so the  day was called wundsdeg or woden's day  eventually turning to wednesday  dies yovis is next named for jupiter the  king of the olympians and god of the sky  the germanic equivalent was thunor or  thor in modern english thor the god of  thunder is perhaps the most famous of  the germanic gods thundra's dag was the  name given which evolved into thursday  the sixth day of the roman week was  called dias veneris named for venus the  roman goddess of beauty and love the  anglo-saxons chose frigg the wife of  odin and goddess of fertility and  motherhood as replacement  in some versions of germanic mythology  she is synonymous with the goddess  freyja who was the goddess of love and  beauty a bit more fitting as a  replacement for venus but in other  versions freya and frigg are two totally  separate goddesses the day was named  friggdag which is now friday  lastly we have saturday which unlike the  other days except arguably sunday and  monday was kept the same named for the  roman titan saturn the old god of  agriculture and father of the first  olympians  i hope you enjoyed learning about the  seven day week before you go i want to  again thank the sponsor of this video  atlas vpn follow the link in the  description below to protect your  internet privacy for just 199 a month  see you next time bye  [Music]
 

